{"blocks":[["Microfreak/UG/03%20Overview/01%20Front%20Panel/02%20Middle%20Row/03%20Analog%20Filter/","source-block-978","High-pass (HPF) attenuates frequencies below cutoff.",["03.01.02.03 Analog filter","The three filter types"]],["Microfreak/UG/03%20Overview/01%20Front%20Panel/02%20Middle%20Row/03%20Analog%20Filter/Asset/01-The-Analog-Filter/png/","source-block-57","01 The Analog Filter",[]],["Microfreak/UG/03%20Overview/01%20Front%20Panel/02%20Middle%20Row/04%20Cycling%20Env/","source-block-282","03.01.02.04 Cycling Envelope",[]],["Microfreak/UG/03%20Overview/01%20Front%20Panel/02%20Middle%20Row/04%20Cycling%20Env/","source-block-315","The Cycling Envelope generates modulation signals for destinations in the Matrix. Unlike a standard envelope, it can retrigger after its last stage finishes. Microfreak/UG/09 Envelope Gen covers its controls.",["03.01.02.04 Cycling Envelope"]],["Microfreak/UG/03%20Overview/01%20Front%20Panel/02%20Middle%20Row/04%20Cycling%20Env/","source-block-531","The Cycling Envelope Generator",["03.01.02.04 Cycling Envelope"]],["Microfreak/UG/03%20Overview/01%20Front%20Panel/02%20Middle%20Row/04%20Cycling%20Env/Asset/01-The-Cycling-Envelope-Generator/png/","source-block-57","01 The Cycling Envelope Generator",[]],["Microfreak/UG/03%20Overview/01%20Front%20Panel/02%20Middle%20Row/Asset/01-Middle-row-of-the-MicroFreak/png/","source-block-57","01 Middle row of the MicroFreak",[]],["Microfreak/UG/03%20Overview/01%20Front%20Panel/03%20Bottom%20Row/","source-block-236","03.01.03 Bottom Row",[]],["Microfreak/UG/03%20Overview/01%20Front%20Panel/03%20Bottom%20Row/","source-block-260","Bottom row of the MicroFreak",["03.01.03 Bottom Row"]],["Microfreak/UG/03%20Overview/01%20Front%20Panel/03%20Bottom%20Row/01%20Octave%20Select/","source-block-208","03.01.03.01 Octave select",[]],["Microfreak/UG/03%20Overview/01%20Front%20Panel/03%20Bottom%20Row/01%20Octave%20Select/","source-block-238","The octave buttons select the active keyboard range.",["03.01.03.01 Octave select"]],["Microfreak/UG/03%20Overview/01%20Front%20Panel/03%20Bottom%20Row/01%20Octave%20Select/","source-block-294","Octave select",["03.01.03.01 Octave select"]],["Microfreak/UG/03%20Overview/01%20Front%20Panel/03%20Bottom%20Row/01%20Octave%20Select/Asset/01-Octave-select/png/","source-block-57","01 Octave select",[]],["Microfreak/UG/03%20Overview/01%20Front%20Panel/03%20Bottom%20Row/02%20Shift/","source-block-293","03.01.03.02 Shift",[]],["Microfreak/UG/03%20Overview/01%20Front%20Panel/03%20Bottom%20Row/02%20Shift/","source-block-315","Hold Shift to access functions printed in blue on the panel and other secondary functions. Microfreak/UG/20 Appendix C - Cheat Sheet lists them.",["03.01.03.02 Shift"]],["Microfreak/UG/03%20Overview/01%20Front%20Panel/03%20Bottom%20Row/02%20Shift/","source-block-471","The shift button",["03.01.03.02 Shift"]],["Microfreak/UG/03%20Overview/01%20Front%20Panel/03%20Bottom%20Row/02%20Shift/","source-block-699","Shift functions",["03.01.03.02 Shift"]],["Microfreak/UG/03%20Overview/01%20Front%20Panel/03%20Bottom%20Row/02%20Shift/","source-block-718","Toggle between Arpeggiator and Sequencer.",["03.01.03.02 Shift","Shift functions"]],["Microfreak/UG/03%20Overview/01%20Front%20Panel/03%20Bottom%20Row/02%20Shift/","source-block-764","Set the swing rate.",["03.01.03.02 Shift","Shift functions"]],["Microfreak/UG/03%20Overview/01%20Front%20Panel/03%20Bottom%20Row/02%20Shift/","source-block-788","Control the Attack and Fall shapes of the Cycling Envelope.",["03.01.03.02 Shift","Shift functions"]],["Microfreak/UG/03%20Overview/01%20Front%20Panel/03%20Bottom%20Row/02%20Shift/","source-block-852","Transpose or reload sequences, or copy an arpeggio to a sequence.",["03.01.03.02 Shift","Shift functions"]],["Microfreak/UG/03%20Overview/01%20Front%20Panel/03%20Bottom%20Row/02%20Shift/Asset/01-The-shift-button/png/","source-block-57","01 The shift button",[]],["Microfreak/UG/03%20Overview/01%20Front%20Panel/03%20Bottom%20Row/03%20Arp%20Seq/","source-block-281","03.01.03.03 ARP/Seq (Arpeggiator/Sequencer)",[]],["Microfreak/UG/03%20Overview/01%20Front%20Panel/03%20Bottom%20Row/03%20Arp%20Seq/","source-block-329","The Arpeggiator plays notes derived from the held keys. Microfreak/UG/12 Arpeggiator and Microfreak/UG/13 Sequencer share several controls.",["03.01.03.03 ARP/Seq (Arpeggiator/Sequencer)"]],["Microfreak/UG/03%20Overview/01%20Front%20Panel/03%20Bottom%20Row/03%20Arp%20Seq/","source-block-480","The Arpeggiator and the Sequencers",["03.01.03.03 ARP/Seq (Arpeggiator/Sequencer)"]],["Microfreak/UG/03%20Overview/01%20Front%20Panel/03%20Bottom%20Row/03%20Arp%20Seq/","source-block-766","Arp | Seq switches between the Arpeggiator and Sequencer. Oct | Mod sets the Arpeggiator range or selects one of four Sequencer modulation tracks.",["03.01.03.03 ARP/Seq (Arpeggiator/Sequencer)"]],["Microfreak/UG/03%20Overview/01%20Front%20Panel/03%20Bottom%20Row/03%20Arp%20Seq/","source-block-924","Rate sets the tempo in BPM. Press the knob to enable Sync; with Sync active, the knob changes the time division relative to the set tempo.",["03.01.03.03 ARP/Seq (Arpeggiator/Sequencer)"]],["Microfreak/UG/03%20Overview/01%20Front%20Panel/03%20Bottom%20Row/03%20Arp%20Seq/Asset/01-The-Arpeggiator-and-the-Sequencers/png/","source-block-57","01 The Arpeggiator and the Sequencers",[]],["Microfreak/UG/03%20Overview/01%20Front%20Panel/03%20Bottom%20Row/04%20LFO/","source-block-287","03.01.03.04 LFO",[]],["Microfreak/UG/03%20Overview/01%20Front%20Panel/03%20Bottom%20Row/04%20LFO/","source-block-307","The low-frequency oscillator produces modulation at 0.05–100 Hz and offers six waveforms.",["03.01.03.04 LFO"]],["Microfreak/UG/03%20Overview/01%20Front%20Panel/03%20Bottom%20Row/04%20LFO/","source-block-402","The LFO",["03.01.03.04 LFO"]],["Microfreak/UG/03%20Overview/01%20Front%20Panel/03%20Bottom%20Row/04%20LFO/","source-block-601","Shape selects a waveform",["03.01.03.04 LFO"]],["Microfreak/UG/03%20Overview/01%20Front%20Panel/03%20Bottom%20Row/04%20LFO/","source-block-633","Sine rises and falls smoothly.",["03.01.03.04 LFO","Shape selects a waveform"]],["Microfreak/UG/03%20Overview/01%20Front%20Panel/03%20Bottom%20Row/04%20LFO/","source-block-668","Triangle rises and falls linearly.",["03.01.03.04 LFO","Shape selects a waveform"]],["Microfreak/UG/03%20Overview/01%20Front%20Panel/03%20Bottom%20Row/04%20LFO/","source-block-707","Rising sawtooth rises linearly and then drops suddenly.",["03.01.03.04 LFO","Shape selects a waveform"]],["Microfreak/UG/03%20Overview/01%20Front%20Panel/03%20Bottom%20Row/04%20LFO/","source-block-767","Square switches suddenly between minimum and maximum.",["03.01.03.04 LFO","Shape selects a waveform"]],["Microfreak/UG/03%20Overview/01%20Front%20Panel/03%20Bottom%20Row/04%20LFO/","source-block-825","Random stepped jumps between randomly generated values.",["03.01.03.04 LFO","Shape selects a waveform"]],["Microfreak/UG/03%20Overview/01%20Front%20Panel/03%20Bottom%20Row/04%20LFO/","source-block-885","Random gliding moves gradually between randomly generated values.",["03.01.03.04 LFO","Shape selects a waveform"]],["Microfreak/UG/03%20Overview/01%20Front%20Panel/03%20Bottom%20Row/04%20LFO/","source-block-955","Rate sets LFO speed. Press it to enable Sync, which follows the Sequencer/Arpeggiator tempo clock. With Sync off, Rate sets the speed independently.",["03.01.03.04 LFO"]],["Microfreak/UG/03%20Overview/01%20Front%20Panel/03%20Bottom%20Row/04%20LFO/Asset/01-The-LFO/png/","source-block-57","01 The LFO",[]],["Microfreak/UG/03%20Overview/01%20Front%20Panel/03%20Bottom%20Row/05%20Gen%20Env/","source-block-284","03.01.03.05 The General Envelope Generator",[]],["Microfreak/UG/03%20Overview/01%20Front%20Panel/03%20Bottom%20Row/05%20Gen%20Env/","source-block-331","The Envelope Generator shapes a tone’s loudness or timbre and can be patched to destinations in the Matrix. Attack, Decay/Release, and Sustain affect the filter by default; Filter Amt sets the envelope’s effect on the filter. Microfreak/UG/09 Envelope Gen explains the controls in detail.",["03.01.03.05 The General Envelope Generator"]],["Microfreak/UG/03%20Overview/01%20Front%20Panel/03%20Bottom%20Row/05%20Gen%20Env/","source-block-647","The Envelope Generator",["03.01.03.05 The General Envelope Generator"]],["Microfreak/UG/03%20Overview/01%20Front%20Panel/03%20Bottom%20Row/05%20Gen%20Env/","source-block-897","With Amp Mod active, the envelope also shapes VCA loudness.",["03.01.03.05 The General Envelope Generator"]],["Microfreak/UG/03%20Overview/01%20Front%20Panel/03%20Bottom%20Row/05%20Gen%20Env/Asset/01-The-Envelope-Generator/png/","source-block-57","01 The Envelope Generator",[]],["Microfreak/UG/03%20Overview/01%20Front%20Panel/03%20Bottom%20Row/06%20Keyboard/","source-block-290","03.01.03.06 Keyboard section",[]],["Microfreak/UG/03%20Overview/01%20Front%20Panel/03%20Bottom%20Row/06%20Keyboard/","source-block-323","The 25-key capacitive keyboard generates gate, pitch, and pressure. The octave buttons extend its two-octave range. The section also includes the Icon strip and the Bend, Spice, and Dice touch controls.",["03.01.03.06 Keyboard section"]],["Microfreak/UG/03%20Overview/01%20Front%20Panel/03%20Bottom%20Row/06%20Keyboard/","source-block-618","The Keyboard",["03.01.03.06 Keyboard section"]],["Microfreak/UG/03%20Overview/01%20Front%20Panel/03%20Bottom%20Row/06%20Keyboard/","source-block-837","Utility or MIDI Control Center settings determine whether the keyboard provides aftertouch or velocity. USB and MIDI out can send fully polyphonic MIDI control to other devices.",["03.01.03.06 Keyboard section"]],["Microfreak/UG/03%20Overview/01%20Front%20Panel/03%20Bottom%20Row/06%20Keyboard/Asset/01-The-Keyboard/png/","source-block-57","01 The Keyboard",[]]],"format_version":5}